<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ben Youssef Madrasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1560s</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ben Youssef <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">Madrasa</a> is an Islamic college in the medina of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a>, founded in the fourteenth century under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> and rebuilt on a larger scale by the Saadi sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-al-ghalib">Abdallah al-Ghalib</a> in the 1560s. Arranged around a courtyard with a pool and about 130 student rooms, it is decorated with carved cedar, stucco and zellij tilework, and was once the largest madrasa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ben-youssef-madrasa.jpg" alt="Ben Youssef Madrasa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang B · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coranic_School_(106589859).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
